Problem: Deque (Double-Ended Queue)

A Deque is a linear data structure that allows insertion and deletion of elements from both the front and the rear. It provides more flexibility than a standard queue or stack.

Common Operations:
1. push_front(value): Insert an element at the front of the deque.
2. push_back(value): Insert an element at the rear of the deque.
3. pop_front(): Remove an element from the front of the deque.
4. pop_back(): Remove an element from the rear of the deque.
5. front(): Return the front element of the deque.
6. back(): Return the rear element of the deque.
7. empty(): Check whether the deque is empty.
8. size(): Return the number of elements in the deque.

Additional Operations:
- clear(): Remove all elements from the deque.
- erase(): Remove one or more elements from the deque.
- swap(): Swap contents of two deques.
- emplace_front(): Insert an element at the front without copying.
- emplace_back(): Insert an element at the rear without copying.
- resize(): Change the size of the deque.
- assign(): Replace elements with new values.
- reverse(): Reverse the order of elements.
- sort(): Sort the elements in ascending order.

Time Complexity:
- push_front, push_back, pop_front, pop_back, front, back, empty, size: O(1)
- clear, erase, resize, assign, reverse: O(n)
- sort: O(n log n)

Input:
- Sequence of deque operations with values (if applicable)

Output:
- Results of operations such as front, back, size, or the final state of the deque after all operations

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdbool.h>

#define MAX 5

int deque[MAX];
int front = -1;
int rear = -1;
int count = 0;

bool isFull() {
    return count == MAX;
}

bool isEmpty() {
    return count == 0;
}

void push_back(int val) {
    if (isFull()) {
        printf("Overflow\n");
        return;
    }
    if (front == -1) front = 0;
    rear = (rear + 1) % MAX; // Circular increment
    deque[rear] = val;
    count++;
}

void push_front(int val) {
    if (isFull()) {
        printf("Overflow\n");
        return;
    }
    if (front == -1) {
        front = 0;
        rear = 0;
    } else {
        front = (front - 1 + MAX) % MAX; // Circular decrement
    }
    deque[front] = val;
    count++;
}

void pop_front() {
    if (isEmpty()) {
        printf("Underflow\n");
        return;
    }
    printf("Popped from front: %d\n", deque[front]);
    front = (front + 1) % MAX;
    count--;
}

void pop_back() {
    if (isEmpty()) {
        printf("Underflow\n");
        return;
    }
    printf("Popped from rear: %d\n", deque[rear]);
    rear = (rear - 1 + MAX) % MAX;
    count--;
}

int get_front() { return isEmpty() ? -1 : deque[front]; }
int get_back() { return isEmpty() ? -1 : deque[rear]; }

int main() {
    push_back(10);
    push_back(20);
    push_front(5);
    
    printf("Front: %d, Rear: %d\n", get_front(), get_back()); // Output: 5, 20
    
    pop_front();
    printf("New Front: %d\n", get_front()); // Output: 10
    
    return 0;
}
